⸻

🖼️ What is a Shared Library?

A shared library is a collection of reusable Jenkins pipeline functions and variables stored in Git.
✅ Reuse logic
✅ Centralize updates
✅ Standardize pipelines

⸻

🖼️ Folder Structure Example

(root)
└── vars/
 └── myPipeline.groovy
└── src/
 └── org/
 └── example/
 └── Utils.groovy
🔹 vars/ – entry points
🔹 src/ – support classes

🖼️ Sample Function (Groovy)

// vars/hello.groovy
def call(String name = 'World') {
 echo "Hello, ${name}!"
}

Use in pipeline:

@Library('my-shared-library') _ 
hello('Neha')

